    "https://brocku.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/brocku_careers/job/St-Catharines-Main-Campus/Administrative-Assistant--Faculty-of-Social-Sciences_JR-1025689-1": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant, Faculty of Social Sciences",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-27\nFull time\n\nBrock University is located on the traditional territory of the Haudenosaunee and Anishinaabe peoples, many of whom continue to live and work here today. This territory is covered by the Upper Canada Treaties and is within the land protected by the Dish with One Spoon Wampum Agreement.  We are one of Canada’s outstanding comprehensive universities, where excellence and innovation thrive! Brock has been proudly recognized as a Hamilton-Niagara Top Employer for eight consecutive years. Brock continues to earn recognition as one of Canada’s Best Employers and one of Canada’s Best Employers for Diversity in 2026. For the second consecutive year, Forbes, in partnership with Statista, also named Brock one of Canada’s Top Employers for Company Culture. At Brock, you will find a welcoming, inclusive community and an exciting range of meaningful career opportunities. Ignite new possibilities for your career. Break through at Brock. Post End Date: November 5, 2026 at 11:59 PM This job advertisement is to fill an existing vacancy in the OSSTF (Employee Group) About the Role: Reporting to the Faculty Service Manager, the Administrative Assistant provides frontline service and comprehensive administrative support to faculty leadership, staff, and students. The incumbent ensures smooth day-to-day operations, effective communication, and administrative support for departmental activities. The incumbent acts as the first point of contact, addresses inquiries, supports administrative and operational processes, and assists with logistics while maintaining compliance with institutional standards. The Administrative Assistant will: Provide day-to-day administrative assistance to academic leadership and faculty members; Coordinate communications, prepare documents and correspondence, and support scheduling needs; Act as a liaison between departments, and other units to facilitate effective administrative supports; Provide data entry and expense transactions processing, including reimbursements and purchasing records; Ensure timely and accurate recording of all financial transactions, submitting Finance/AP or through financial systems as appropriate; Review and process faculty and departmental travel and expense reports, including submissions related to meetings, conferences, luncheons, events, and recruitment activities; Maintain records, filing systems, tracking, and databases in accordance with privacy guidelines; Support student award processes and maintain accurate filing systems and databases; Assist with postings and contracts in Workday (e.g., TAs, RAs, overloads), ensuring compliance with collective agreements; Serve as the first point of contact for faculty, staff, and students, responding to inquiries and processing frequent requests; Manage generic email accounts, answer general questions, redirect inquiries, and provide accurate information to ensure timely communication; Schedule department and committee meetings, prepare agendas, and record minutes; Plan and manage logistics for events, workshops, colloquia, and conferences hosted by the program, including guest speakers, student research days, high school visits, and alumni events. Key Skills and Experience: Diploma or degree in a related discipline. The equivalent combination of education and experience would be considered; Experience in administrative or office support role; Proficiency with computer systems and software applications; Ability and willingness to learn and adapt to emerging technologies, including AI tools and platforms; Ability to maintain accurate records, including file retention and tracking; Excellent writing, grammar, editing, and proofreading skills; Promotes and embodies inclusivity and respect within the workplace and the broader community; Excellent communication and interpersonal skills; Ability to provide responsive and professional support to faculty, staff, and students; Works cooperatively with colleagues to achieve departmental goals; Strong organizational and time-management skills with attention to detail; Ability to maintain precise records and manages complex schedules effectively; and Responds effectively to changing priorities and peak workload periods. Salary and Benefit Information: Job Grade H, Salary Scale ($46,099-$63,950)*; This position includes full comprehensive benefits including tuition waiver. This position will be required to work on site 5 days per week. This position is included in the Ontario Secondary School Teachers Federation (OSSTF) Union and: Salary is therefore determined by the OSSTF Collective agreement. * New members shall be placed on the salary grid at the entry level. * It is Brock University’s policy to give first consideration to qualified internal Brock University OSSTF applicants. We are committed to offering flexible work arrangements where possible as outlined in our Flexible Work Arrangement Policy . As a student-centered organization, all employees are required to work on campus as needed.   Brock University is committed to creating a respectful and equitable workplace. We strive to foster a culture of diversity and inclusion in our work and learning environments. We welcome applications from all qualified individuals and actively encourage applications from women, people with disabilities, members of the 2SLGBTQIA+ community, Indigenous Peoples, people who identify as Black, African and/or Caribbean, as racialized and/or as from ethnic and cultural minority groups, and other underrepresented demographic groups at Brock and in the Niagara region. Brock also recognizes intersectionality and the interconnected identities, histories, and experiences of these aforementioned groups .   We are committed to inclusive and barrier-free recruitment, and we accommodat e the needs of applicants throughout all stages of the recruitment process, as outlined in our Employment Accommodation Policy and consistent with the requirements of the Ontario Human Rights Code . Please contact talent@brocku.ca   if you require a disability related accommodation so we can ensure you r participation needs are met.   Brock University does not use AI Technology at any stage of the recruitment process.   We appreciate all applications received . C andidates that are selected for an interview will be contacted.   Learn more about Brock University by visiting www.brocku.ca ."
    },
    "https://brocku.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/brocku_careers/job/St-Catharines-Main-Campus/Teaching-Assistant-AHSC-5P37-Winter-D3_JR-1025688": {
      "title": "Teaching Assistant AHSC 5P37 Winter D3",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-27\nPart time\n\nBrock University is located on the traditional territory of the Haudenosaunee and Anishinaabe peoples, many of whom continue to live and work here today. This territory is covered by the Upper Canada Treaties and is within the land protected by the Dish with One Spoon Wampum Agreement.  We are one of Canada’s outstanding comprehensive universities, where excellence and innovation thrive! Brock has been proudly recognized as a Hamilton-Niagara Top Employer for eight consecutive years. Brock continues to earn recognition as one of Canada’s Best Employers and one of Canada’s Best Employers for Diversity in 2026. For the second consecutive year, Forbes, in partnership with Statista, also named Brock one of Canada’s Top Employers for Company Culture. At Brock, you will find a welcoming, inclusive community and an exciting range of meaningful career opportunities. Ignite new possibilities for your career. Break through at Brock. Post End Date: November 11, 2026 at 11:59 PM This job advertisement is to fill an existing vacancy in the CUPE4207-1 (Employee Group) AHSC 5P37 D3 ANOVAs: Analysis and Interpretation Compensation  Teaching Assistant, Course Coordinator and Lab Demonstrator positions are paid according to the qualifications that the employee holds.   Employees who do NOT hold a 4-year honours degree or a 3-year pass degree will be paid the undergraduate rate - $23.30 per hour.  (Rate effective September 1, 2026)   Employees who hold a 4-year honours degree or a 3-year pass degree will be paid the graduate rate - $36.67 per hour.  (Rate effective September 1, 2026)   In cases where additional duties are required as part of a Teaching Assistant’s duties, these hours shall be compensated at the appropriate Teaching Assistant rate.   Duties  The duties and responsibilities of the Teaching Assistant shall be in accordance with Article 22 of the CUPE Local 4207, Unit 1, Collective Agreement. These are made up of scheduled contact time with students and non-classroom time (including preparation of seminar material, student consultation, marking or grading, examination proctoring, attending lectures, holding office hours, and other course administration as may be required. Qualifications  1. MA or MSc in Applied Health Sciences or related discipline. 2. Experience in teaching a variety of ANOVA-based statistical analysis techniques in research. 3. Evidence of competent and effective teaching experience at the university level. Applications  Please include a cover letter and a current resume. Members with seniority can provide seniority date within the application questionnaire.  For further information  Joanne Kremble Graduate Program Coordinator ahsgradstudies@brocku.ca Positions listed on this posting are subject to course enrolments and budgetary approval.  As per Article 22.04 of the Collective Agreement:  Members shall not accept any appointment which, taken together with all other appointments at the University, would cause the member to exceed the maximum number of regular hours (i.e., not overtime hours) allowable in a work week under the Employment Standards Act, as amended from time to time.  The Collective Agreement governs part-time Instructor, Teaching Assistant, Lab Demonstrator, Course Coordinator and Marker-Grader positions at Brock University. The Agreement can be accessed on the Office of People & Culture website -  https://brocku.ca/human-resources/collective-agreements/   Additional Comments  Course descriptions can be found on the Undergraduate course calendar website:  http://www.brocku.ca/webcal/   Academic terms generally run from: Fall – September to December Winter – January to April Spring – May to July Summer – July to August *Actual dates can be found on the Timetables available on the Office of the Registrar web page: https://brocku.ca/registrar/toolkit/registration/ We are committed to offering flexible work arrangements where possible as outlined in our Flexible Work Arrangement Policy . As a student-centered organization, all employees are required to work on campus as needed.   Brock University is committed to creating a respectful and equitable workplace. We strive to foster a culture of diversity and inclusion in our work and learning environments. We welcome applications from all qualified individuals and actively encourage applications from women, people with disabilities, members of the 2SLGBTQIA+ community, Indigenous Peoples, people who identify as Black, African and/or Caribbean, as racialized and/or as from ethnic and cultural minority groups, and other underrepresented demographic groups at Brock and in the Niagara region. Brock also recognizes intersectionality and the interconnected identities, histories, and experiences of these aforementioned groups .   We are committed to inclusive and barrier-free recruitment, and we accommodat e the needs of applicants throughout all stages of the recruitment process, as outlined in our Employment Accommodation Policy and consistent with the requirements of the Ontario Human Rights Code . Please contact talent@brocku.ca   if you require a disability related accommodation so we can ensure you r participation needs are met.   Brock University does not use AI Technology at any stage of the recruitment process.   We appreciate all applications received . C andidates that are selected for an interview will be contacted.   Learn more about Brock University by visiting www.brocku.ca ."
